-- ako/mxcli#1833 (mendixlabs/mxcli#1684): two defects of `--mcp`, found while
-- checking a report that `exec --mcp` wrote the .mpr instead of Studio Pro.
--
-- 1. `--mcp-trace` / `--mcp-verbose` printed each statement but no PED call:
--    the MCP backend the CLI builds never got the tracer. A run that sent the
--    write to Studio Pro read as one that sent nothing.
-- 2. Without `--mcp-dial`, a `localhost` URL was dialled as
--    host.docker.internal whenever that name resolved. Docker Desktop for
--    Windows adds it to the hosts file (the LAN address), so on the machine
--    Studio Pro runs on the connection timed out: `dial tcp <LAN IP>:7782`.
-- 3. A `localhost` URL was dialled through the resolver, which on the reporter's
--    machine answered with a LAN address first; Studio Pro on Windows listens
--    on 127.0.0.1 only. localhost now dials 127.0.0.1 first and keeps the
--    `Host: localhost` header Studio Pro requires.
--
-- The headline claim — exec / -c with --mcp write the .mpr and mprcontents/
-- and skip the .mpr.lock refusal — does not reproduce: the CLI with --mcp
-- calls ped_create_document and leaves every model file byte-identical, with
-- the lock present; a statement with no PED route (e.g. `create image
-- collection`) is refused, not written. cmd/mxcli/mcp_exec_no_file_write_test.go
-- pins both, with the fault forced back in as its control.
--
-- To verify, with Studio Pro open on a throwaway app and its MCP server on 7782:
--   mxcli exec 1833-mcp-trace-and-dial.mdl -p App.mpr --mcp http://localhost:7782/mcp --mcp-trace
-- The trace lists `→ ped_create_document` and `→ ped_check_errors` under the
-- statement, and the connection needs no --mcp-dial (on Windows, with or
-- without Docker Desktop). The constant appears in Studio Pro's App Explorer,
-- and a hash of App.mpr + mprcontents/ taken before and after is unchanged
-- until Studio Pro itself saves.

mdl 1;

create constant MyFirstModule.McpTraceProbe (Type: String, DefaultValue: 'probe');
